{"html":"<p>Every Java program stores values and does something with them. Before classes and collections, you need the basics: how to declare a variable, which type to pick, and the few operators that behave differently from what you might expect.</p>\n<h2 id=\"variables\">Variables</h2>\n<p>A variable has a <strong>type</strong>, a <strong>name</strong> and a <strong>value</strong>:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> age</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 30</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">String</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> name</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"Ana\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Java is <strong>statically typed</strong>: the type is fixed when you declare the variable, and the compiler refuses wrong values. <code>age = &quot;thirty&quot;;</code> doesn&#39;t compile.</p>\n<p>Since Java 10, <code>var</code> lets the compiler infer the type from the value. The variable still has a fixed type, you just don&#39;t write it:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">var</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> city</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"Lyon\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// city is a String</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Use <code>var</code> when the type is obvious from the right side, and write the type when it helps the reader.</p>\n<p><code>final</code> makes a variable that can&#39;t be reassigned:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">final</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> maxUsers</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 100</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h2 id=\"the-eight-primitive-types\">The Eight Primitive Types</h2>\n<div data-table-scroll><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Holds</th>\n<th>Example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>int</code></td>\n<td>Whole numbers, about ±2.1 billion</td>\n<td><code>int age = 30;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>long</code></td>\n<td>Bigger whole numbers</td>\n<td><code>long people = 8_100_000_000L;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>double</code></td>\n<td>Decimal numbers</td>\n<td><code>double price = 19.99;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>float</code></td>\n<td>Less precise decimals (rarely used)</td>\n<td><code>float ratio = 0.5f;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>boolean</code></td>\n<td><code>true</code> or <code>false</code></td>\n<td><code>boolean active = true;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>char</code></td>\n<td>One character</td>\n<td><code>char grade = &#39;A&#39;;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>byte</code></td>\n<td>Small whole numbers, -128 to 127</td>\n<td>Raw binary data</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>short</code></td>\n<td>Whole numbers up to ±32,767</td>\n<td>Rarely used</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p>In practice you&#39;ll mostly use <code>int</code>, <code>long</code>, <code>double</code> and <code>boolean</code>. Underscores in numbers, like <code>8_100_000_000L</code>, are only for readability. The <code>L</code> marks a <code>long</code> literal.</p>\n<h2 id=\"string\">String</h2>\n<p><code>String</code> isn&#39;t a primitive: it&#39;s a class, but Java gives it special syntax. Strings are <strong>immutable</strong>: methods like <code>toUpperCase()</code> return a new string instead of changing the old one.</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">String</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> name</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"Ana\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(name </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \" is \"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 30</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// Ana is 30</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Compare strings with <code>equals</code>, never <code>==</code>. <code>==</code> checks whether two variables point to the <strong>same object</strong>, not whether the text is the same:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">String</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> s1</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"java\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">String</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> s2</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> String</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"java\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(s1 </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">==</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> s2);       </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// false</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(s1.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">equals</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(s2));  </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// true</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h2 id=\"arithmetic-and-its-traps\">Arithmetic and Its Traps</h2>\n<p>The usual operators work as expected: <code>+</code>, <code>-</code>, <code>*</code>, <code>/</code>, and <code>%</code> for the remainder. Three traps catch every beginner.</p>\n<h3 id=\"integer-division\">Integer Division</h3>\n<p>Dividing two <code>int</code>s gives an <code>int</code>: the decimals are dropped, not rounded.</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">7</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> /</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);            </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 3</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">7</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> %</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);            </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 1</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">7</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> /</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 2.0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);          </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 3.5</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">double</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">7</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> /</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 3.5</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>If either side is a <code>double</code>, the result is a <code>double</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"overflow\">Overflow</h3>\n<p>An <code>int</code> that goes past its maximum silently wraps around to the most negative value:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> big</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Integer.MAX_VALUE;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(big </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// -2147483648</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Use <code>long</code> for values that can grow large, like money in cents or timestamps, or <code>Math.addExact</code>, which throws instead of wrapping.</p>\n<h3 id=\"decimals-aren-t-exact\">Decimals Aren&#39;t Exact</h3>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">0.1</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 0.2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 0.30000000000000004</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p><code>double</code> stores numbers in binary, and 0.1 has no exact binary form. Never use <code>double</code> for money: use <code>long</code> cents or <code>BigDecimal</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"string-concatenation-order\">String Concatenation Order</h3>\n<p><code>+</code> works left to right, so once a string is involved, numbers are glued as text:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Total: \"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);     </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// Total: 12</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Total: \"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">));   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// Total: 3</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h2 id=\"shortcuts-and\">Shortcuts: +=, ++ and --</h2>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 5</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">x </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+=</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 3</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// x = x + 3, now 8</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">x</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">++</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;      </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// now 9</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p><code>x++</code> gives the old value, then adds one; <code>++x</code> adds one first:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> a</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 5</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> b</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> a</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">++</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// b is 5, a is 6</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> ++</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">a;   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// a is 7, c is 7</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Keep <code>++</code> on its own line and you&#39;ll never have to remember this.</p>\n<h2 id=\"comparing-and-combining\">Comparing and Combining</h2>\n<p>Comparisons give a <code>boolean</code>: <code>==</code>, <code>!=</code>, <code>&lt;</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;=</code>, <code>&gt;=</code>.</p>\n<p>Combine them with <code>&amp;&amp;</code> (and), <code>||</code> (or) and <code>!</code> (not):</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">10</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> ></span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 3</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> &#x26;&#x26;</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 2</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> ></span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 5</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// false</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">10</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> ></span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 3</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> ||</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 2</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> ></span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 5</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// true</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p><code>&amp;&amp;</code> and <code>||</code> stop early: in <code>a != null &amp;&amp; a.isEmpty()</code>, the second part only runs when <code>a</code> isn&#39;t null, which prevents a <code>NullPointerException</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"converting-between-types\">Converting Between Types</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Widening</strong> is automatic: an <code>int</code> fits in a <code>long</code> or a <code>double</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Narrowing</strong> needs a cast, and can lose data: <code>(int) 9.99</code> is <code>9</code>, cut, not rounded. Use <code>Math.round</code> to round.</li>\n<li><strong>Text to numbers:</strong> <code>Integer.parseInt(&quot;42&quot;)</code>, <code>Double.parseDouble(&quot;3.5&quot;)</code>. They throw a <code>NumberFormatException</code> on bad input.</li>\n<li><strong>Numbers to text:</strong> <code>String.valueOf(3.5)</code>, or <code>&quot;&quot; + 3.5</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-answer-in-short\">The Answer in Short</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Declare variables with a type, or <code>var</code> when the type is obvious; <code>final</code> stops reassignment.</li>\n<li>Use <code>int</code>, <code>long</code>, <code>double</code> and <code>boolean</code> for most values; <code>String</code> is a class and immutable.</li>\n<li>Compare strings with <code>equals</code>, not <code>==</code>.</li>\n<li>Watch integer division, <code>int</code> overflow and decimal rounding; use <code>long</code> or <code>BigDecimal</code> for money.</li>\n<li><code>&amp;&amp;</code> and <code>||</code> stop early; narrowing casts cut data, and parsing can throw.</li>\n</ol>\n"}